an important role in testicular development and spermatogenesis (PubMed:16955368). In addition to its role on endogenous nucleotides, it deaminates the active triphosphate forms of the cytidine analog drugs, gemcitabine (dFdCTP) and decitabine (5-aza-dCTP), rendering them susceptible to inactivation by deoxyuridine triphosphatase (DUT). This process limits drug-induced cytotoxicity and contributes to cellular resistance to gemcitabine and decitabine (PubMed:40504152)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}